{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Seventh turn: the contrast experiment ran (CheckRun 8e0e2faf9e154895917c055c2a439623, completed, exit_code 0) and its raw measurements parsed, but both declared comparisons came back unknown: the admission events did not carry the same identity fields as the comparisons ('Ambiguous prerequisite association; missing admitted_nosnap.use_snapshots', 'Missing operation admission fields or identity' on the state_reached events). The harness is corrected by emitting use_snapshots on every event and by declaring identity on the case name alone, then resubmitted as a fresh revision of the same experiment; no measurement path is changed.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\": {\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"assurance_gap.rs\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"follower_prepare\\\",\\\"logsync\\\",\\\"memstorage_suffix\\\",\\\"storage_get_suffix_contract\\\",\\\"sync_log\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\": {\n   \\\"description\\\": \\\"Two single-node scenarios in one test: a responder replica is driven through a legal leader prefix (Prepare, AcceptSync with six entries and decided_idx 6, forwarded Compaction::Trim(6)) and then receives a legal Prepare with decided_idx 3 and an older accepted round. Everything is held equal except the Entry type: one scenario has Snapshot::use_snapshots() == false, the other true. The outcome of handling that Prepare is reported per case.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n    \\\"The messages delivered are the shapes a real leader produces (Prepare, AcceptSync/log_sync, forwarded Compaction::Trim, and a later Prepare from a node whose decided index lags); the responder is a real OmniPaxos instance whose state is produced by those messages rather than set directly.\\\",\n    \\\"The three-node configuration is used only for construction; the responder is node 2 and the sender is node 1. No tick, no election and no message routing are involved, so nothing depends on scheduling.\\\",\n    \\\"AcceptSync carries sync_idx 0 with a six-entry suffix and decided_idx 6, i.e. the update a leader sends to a peer that has no entries yet; the forwarded Trim(6) is legal because the responder's decided index is already 6.\\\",\n    \\\"The state this harness reaches (accepted_idx 6, decided_idx 6, compacted_idx 6, accepted round newer than the preparing node's) is the same state the earlier multi-node experiment reached through real message exchange.\\\",\n    \\\"Dev profile with overflow checks enabled, matching the controller's cargo test invocation.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"excluded\\\": [\n    \\\"Release-profile behaviour, the persistent storage backend, and cluster-level consequences after the abort are not measured here.\\\",\n    \\\"Only the snapshot/non-snapshot distinction is varied; cluster size, batch size, trim index and quorum are held equal.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"parameters\\\": {\\\"responder_pid\\\":2,\\\"sender_pid\\\":1,\\\"entries_synced\\\":6,\\\"trim_idx\\\":6,\\\"stale_decided_idx\\\":3,\\\"cases\\\":[\\\"nosnapshot_entry\\\",\\\"snapshot_entry\\\"]}\n  },\n  \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"scenario(case, snapshots) builds one OmniPaxos instance (pid 2, nodes 1,2,3, MemoryStorage behind a shared handle) and then calls, in order: handle_incoming(Prepare{n: (1,1,pid 1), decided_idx: 0, n_accepted: 0, accepted_idx: 0}); handle_incoming(AcceptSync{n: (1,1,pid 1), seq_num: (session 0, counter 1), decided_idx: 6, log_sync: {decided_snapshot: None, suffix: six entries 0..5, sync_idx: 0, stopsign: None}}); handle_incoming(Compaction::Trim(6)). It then emits case_started and state_reached (both carrying case and use_snapshots, plus accepted_idx/decided_idx/compacted_idx on state_reached), and finally calls handle_incoming(Prepare{n: (1,2,pid 1), decided_idx: 3, n_accepted: 0, accepted_idx: 6}) inside catch_unwind, emitting log_sync_outcome with case, use_snapshots, outcome, panic message and the three indices. The test runs this twice: case nosnapshot_entry (use_snapshots() == false) and case snapshot_entry (use_snapshots() == true, a max-value snapshot type).\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\": [\\\"No production logic is replaced or patched; the harness only uses the crate's public API and message types. Relative to the previous revision only the emitted identity fields changed (use_snapshots added to state_reached).\\\"],\n  \\\"responsibility\\\": \\\"The contrast isolates which captured component decides the outcome: the core's log-update construction selects its branch from T::Snapshot::use_snapshots() and the deciding node's decided index, and the captured in-memory storage implementation aborts on an index below its trimmed prefix.\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\": \\\"f35a1f8caebf4d9495c2b22026b373d9-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\": \\\"Admission identity fix: state_reached did not emit use_snapshots, so prerequisite correlation for both comparisons failed (unknown outcome) even though the measurements were observed. The harness now emits case and use_snapshots on every event; the message sequence, node configuration and measured endpoint are unchanged.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\": [\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admitted_nosnap\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"state_reached\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"case\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nosnapshot_entry\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"use_snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"accepted_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"decided_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"compacted_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admitted_snap\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"state_reached\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"case\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"snapshot_entry\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"use_snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"accepted_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"decided_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"compacted_idx\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":6}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\": [\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"log_sync_outcome\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admitted_nosnap\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"outcome\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Without snapshots, handling the stale node's Prepare completes instead of aborting.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"log_sync_outcome\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admitted_snap\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"outcome\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},\\\"description\\\":\\\"With snapshots enabled, the same request completes, bounding the failure to the non-snapshot configuration.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the snapshot branch is taken only when use_snapshots() is true and decided_idx > common_prefix_idx; otherwise get_suffix(common_prefix_idx) is used with no comparison against the responder's compacted index\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(d, open('update.json','w'), indent=2)\nprint(\\\"written\\\")\nEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
